or of the company  you keep jeffrey cohen the author of see  no evil the backstage battle over sex  and violence in television will be the  moderator and another one of the  speakers will be david maranist who  wrote they marched into sunlight warren  peace vietnam and america october 1967.  mr marianis is up for one of the awards  tonight the la times festival of the  books will be giving out awards tonight  uh just the back of us in uh royce hall  and uh we'll know a little bit more  about who those awards are and we'll be  able to tell you about them tomorrow in  our last segment tonight please stay  with us because we're going to take  phone calls for lou cannon liu cannon  wrote the book of course about lots of  books actually on ronald reagan he has  written a lot of biographical work but  his newest work is about ronald reagan  in this state and how that was the  beginnings of his national career so all  of that coming up today and then we'll  be live again here tomorrow uh there's a  280 exhibitors and also quite a few  other people uh exhibiting and writing  and so we will take you back inside  haynes auditorium now  for our live coverage of this next panel
 

